@page "/components/treeview"

<DocsPage>
    <DocsPageHeader Title="Tree View" Component="@nameof(MudTreeView<T>)">
        <Description>A highly‑customizable component for visualising hierarchical data with rich selection, lazy‑loading, filtering, and templating features.</Description>
    </DocsPageHeader>

    <DocsPageContent>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Basic">
                <Description>
                    <strong>MudTreeView</strong> renders parent‑child hierarchies.<br /><br />

                    <ul>
                        <li>Every <CodeInline Tag>MudTreeViewItem</CodeInline> shows a <CodeInline>Text</CodeInline> label and can carry a typed <CodeInline>Value</CodeInline>.</li>
                        <li>If <CodeInline>T</CodeInline> is <CodeInline>string</CodeInline> and you omit <CodeInline>Value</CodeInline>, the label is also stored as the value.</li>
                        <li>If you omit <CodeInline>Text</CodeInline> but set <CodeInline>Value</CodeInline>, the label is taken from <CodeInline>Value.ToString()</CodeInline>.</li>
                        <li>You can set both to display a friendly label while storing a different value—handy when <CodeInline>T</CodeInline> is an object.</li>
                    </ul><br />

                    In the demo below <CodeInline>ReadOnly="true"</CodeInline>, so you can explore the data without a selection highlight. Some items have only text, some have only a value and one has both—observe how the control renders each case.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewBasicExample)" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Usage">
                <Description>
                    Behaviour flags:<br /><br />

                    <ul>
                        <li><CodeInline>Hover</CodeInline> - highlight on pointer‑over.</li>
                        <li><CodeInline>Ripple</CodeInline> - click ripple (ignored when <CodeInline>ExpandOnDoubleClick</CodeInline> is true).</li>
                        <li><CodeInline>Dense</CodeInline> - compact vertical padding.</li>
                        <li><CodeInline>Disabled</CodeInline> - block all interaction.</li>
                    </ul><br />

                    Expansion:<br /><br />

                    <ul>
                        <li><CodeInline>ExpandOnClick</CodeInline> - single‑click toggles a branch.</li>
                        <li><CodeInline>ExpandOnDoubleClick</CodeInline> - double‑click toggles a branch and fires <CodeInline>OnDoubleClick</CodeInline>. When set, it overrides single‑click expansion.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewUsageExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Icons">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Node icon: <CodeInline>Icon</CodeInline></li>
                        <li>Icon colour: <CodeInline>IconColor</CodeInline></li>
                        <li>Expand/collapse button: <CodeInline>ExpandButtonIcon</CodeInline></li>
                        <li>Alternative icon when expanded: <CodeInline>IconExpanded</CodeInline></li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewIconExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Single Selection">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li><CodeInline>SelectionMode.SingleSelection</CodeInline> - exactly one node can be selected.</li>
                        <li><CodeInline>SelectionMode.ToggleSelection</CodeInline> - clicking the selected node again clears the selection.</li>
                        <li>Use <CodeInline>@@bind-SelectedValue</CodeInline> to read or set the current value.</li>
                        <li>Adjust highlight colour with <CodeInline>Color</CodeInline>.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewSingleSelectionExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Multi Selection">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li><CodeInline>SelectionMode.MultiSelection</CodeInline> - checkboxes allow picking multiple nodes.</li>
                        <li>Bind to <CodeInline>@@bind-SelectedValues</CodeInline> to track the set.</li>
                        <li>Change checkbox colour with <CodeInline>CheckBoxColor</CodeInline>.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewMultiSelectionExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Binding Items Directly">
                <Description>
                    Bind <CodeInline>Selected</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>Expanded</CodeInline> on individual <CodeInline Tag>MudTreeViewItem</CodeInline> components for fine‑grained control—especially useful when you create nodes via <CodeInline>ItemTemplate</CodeInline>.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewBindItemsExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Auto‑Expand">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li><CodeInline>AutoExpand="true"</CodeInline> - when a collapsed branch gains a selected descendant it opens automatically.</li>
                        <li>Call <CodeInline>ExpandAll()</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>CollapseAll()</CodeInline> on the component reference to open or close every level.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewAutoExpandExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Item Template">
                <Description>
                    <CodeInline>ItemTemplate</CodeInline> builds nodes from your model. The template receives the data item so you can render custom markup, choose icons, or forward the model to child levels.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewItemTemplateExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Server‑Side Data & Lazy Loading">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Populate children on demand through async <CodeInline>ServerData</CodeInline>. The tree calls it the first time a node with no children expands.</li>
                        <li>Show a custom spinner with <CodeInline>LoadingIcon</CodeInline> and <CodeInline>LoadingIconColor</CodeInline>.</li>
                        <li>If a node is known to be a leaf, set <CodeInline>CanExpand="false"</CodeInline> to skip the network call.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewServerExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Filtering">
                <Description>
                    Provide <CodeInline>FilterFunc</CodeInline> to decide visibility node‑by‑node, then call <CodeInline>Filter()</CodeInline> to apply it—the method toggles each node’s <CodeInline>Visible</CodeInline> flag.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewFilteringExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Custom Look & Behaviour">
                <Description>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Set <CodeInline>Content</CodeInline> on a <CodeInline Tag>MudTreeViewItem</CodeInline> to replace its default layout completely.</li>
                        <li>The demo below implements non‑cascading multi‑selection where parent and child selections are independent.</li>
                        <li>For smooth scrolling, constrain the container’s <CodeInline>height</CodeInline> or <CodeInline>max‑height</CodeInline> and set <CodeInline>overflow‑y: auto</CodeInline>.</li>
                    </ul>
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Code="@nameof(TreeViewCustomExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Custom Body Content">
                <Description>
                    Use <CodeInline Tag>BodyContent</CodeInline> when you only need to customise the body while keeping built‑in icons and the expander button.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
            <SectionContent Outlined="true" Code="@nameof(TreeViewBodyContentExample)" ShowCode="false" />
        </DocsPageSection>

    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>
